// @emit-error cannot be discriminated
// The `same-field-names-i32-vs-boolean-reject.vl` rule at the pair the SAME exemption
// swallowed one type over. `assignTags` refuses two variants that share a field-NAME set —
// `variantSig`, the tag key, IS that set — unless they are one variant reached through two
// spellings, and that exemption compares the fields' identity text (`uFieldTyText`).
//
// A bare literal annotation renders through canon as its SOFTENED base, so `kind: "circle"`
// and `kind: "rect"` both recorded the text `string`, compared EQUAL, and were folded as the
// layout-equal twin the exemption exists to admit. Measured on the branch that admitted these
// arms without the identity rung: `vl check` rc 0, `vl run` rc 0, printing the `C` branch for
// a value built through `R` — a SILENT wrong answer, and the inverted spelling is wrong the
// same way, so no construction decides it.
//
// The identity column now carries the literal itself (`"circle"` / `"rect"`, quoted so a
// literal `"i32"` tag cannot collide with the type `i32` in a raw-text comparison), so the
// pair reaches the same reject its NAMED spelling has always taken — `type KC = "circle"`
// records `KC` / `KR` in both the identity and the elem-name column and rejects on master.
//
// WHY THIS IS A REJECT AND NOT A FEATURE. VL's structural unions discriminate on the field-NAME
// set (`docs/guide/unions.md`); a tag VALUE is not a runtime discriminator, because a bare
// literal field stores as a plain string slot. Making this pair work needs the tag to carry an
// interned identity — the un-named-literal ATOM rep, A5c — which is a representation decision,
// not a widening of this exemption. Until then the correct column for it is LOUD.
//
// The layout-equal twin the exemption is FOR is unaffected: two arms whose tag literals are
// the SAME are still one variant and still fold — `variant-twin-scalar-spellings.vl`.

type C = { kind: "circle", size: f64 }
type R = { kind: "rect", size: f64 }
type S = C | R

const c: S = { kind: "rect", size: 2.0 }
if c is C { print("C") } else { print("R") }
